  "adaptation": "Retain WinOne module namespace, unified configuration/logs/tray, recovery errors and PID-reuse protection. Reuse scoped Esc/native-close handling, script identity, original-window visibility and queued tray gestures. Existing WinOne native console creation retains its explicit environment/ownership handling. UI uses existing WinOne controls; program exit requires confirmation. Manual launch settings stay independent from the startup switch; collected-icon single click still automatically adds a double click. No new dependency or standalone WinTray UI. Tray collection uses the same local WinTray receiving-end bridge; WinOne permits EPOCH/RESUME through its per-window UIPI filter for elevated operation and preserves native handshake errors instead of reporting every delivery failure as a timeout."
